#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--commit`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-commit`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Perform the merge and commit the result. This option can be used to override "
"`--no-commit`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:7
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:100
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:145
#, no-wrap
msgid "\tOnly useful when merging.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:12
msgid ""
"With `--no-commit` perform the merge and stop just before creating a merge "
"commit, to give the user a chance to inspect and further tweak the merge "
"result before committing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:17
msgid ""
"Note that fast-forward updates do not create a merge commit and therefore "
"there is no way to stop those merges with `--no-commit`.  Thus, if you want "
"to ensure your branch is not changed or updated by the merge command, use "
"`--no-ff` with `--no-commit`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--edit`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-e`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-edit`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:26
msgid ""
"Invoke an editor before committing successful mechanical merge to further "
"edit the auto-generated merge message, so that the user can explain and "
"justify the merge. The `--no-edit` option can be used to accept the "
"auto-generated message (this is generally discouraged)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:30
msgid ""
"The `--edit` (or `-e`) option is still useful if you are giving a draft "
"message with the `-m` option from the command line and want to edit it in "
"the editor."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:37
msgid ""
"Older scripts may depend on the historical behaviour of not allowing the "
"user to edit the merge log message. They will see an editor opened when they "
"run `git merge`. To make it easier to adjust such scripts to the updated "
"behaviour, the environment variable `GIT_MERGE_AUTOEDIT` can be set to `no` "
"at the beginning of them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--cleanup=<mode>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:44
msgid ""
"This option determines how the merge message will be cleaned up before "
"committing. See linkgit:git-commit[1] for more details. In addition, if the "
"_<mode>_ is given a value of `scissors`, scissors will be appended to "
"`MERGE_MSG` before being passed on to the commit machinery in the case of a "
"merge conflict."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:46
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--ff`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:47
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-ff`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:48
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--ff-only`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:54
msgid ""
"Specifies how a merge is handled when the merged-in history is already a "
"descendant of the current history.  `--ff` is the default unless merging an "
"annotated (and possibly signed) tag that is not stored in its natural place "
"in the `refs/tags/` hierarchy, in which case `--no-ff` is assumed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:60
msgid ""
"Only update to the new history if there is no divergent local history.  This "
"is the default when no method for reconciling divergent histories is "
"provided (via the --rebase=* flags)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:69
msgid ""
"When merging rather than rebasing, specifies how a merge is handled when the "
"merged-in history is already a descendant of the current history.  If "
"merging is requested, `--ff` is the default unless merging an annotated (and "
"possibly signed) tag that is not stored in its natural place in the "
"`refs/tags/` hierarchy, in which case `--no-ff` is assumed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:75
msgid ""
"With `--ff`, when possible resolve the merge as a fast-forward (only update "
"the branch pointer to match the merged branch; do not create a merge "
"commit).  When not possible (when the merged-in history is not a descendant "
"of the current history), create a merge commit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:78
msgid ""
"With `--no-ff`, create a merge commit in all cases, even when the merge "
"could instead be resolved as a fast-forward."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:82
msgid ""
"With `--ff-only`, resolve the merge as a fast-forward when possible.  When "
"not possible, refuse to merge and exit with a non-zero status."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:84
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-S[<key-id>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:85
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--gpg-sign[=<key-id>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-gpg-sign`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:92
msgid ""
"GPG-sign the resulting merge commit. The _<key-id>_ argument is optional and "
"defaults to the committer identity; if specified, it must be stuck to the "
"option without a space. `--no-gpg-sign` is useful to countermand both "
"`commit.gpgSign` configuration variable, and earlier `--gpg-sign`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:93
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--log[=<n>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-log`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:98
msgid ""
"In addition to branch names, populate the log message with one-line "
"descriptions from at most _<n>_ actual commits that are being merged. See "
"also linkgit:git-fmt-merge-msg[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:104
msgid ""
"With `--no-log` do not list one-line descriptions from the actual commits "
"being merged."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--stat`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:108
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-n`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-stat`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:112
msgid ""
"Show a diffstat at the end of the merge. The diffstat is also controlled by "
"the configuration option merge.stat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:115
msgid "With `-n` or `--no-stat` do not show a diffstat at the end of the merge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--compact-summary`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:118
msgid "Show a compact-summary at the end of the merge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:119
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--squash`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-squash`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:128
msgid ""
"Produce the working tree and index state as if a real merge happened (except "
"for the merge information), but do not actually make a commit, move the "
"`HEAD`, or record `$GIT_DIR/MERGE_HEAD` (to cause the next `git commit` "
"command to create a merge commit).  This allows you to create a single "
"commit on top of the current branch whose effect is the same as merging "
"another branch (or more in case of an octopus)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:131
msgid ""
"With `--no-squash` perform the merge and commit the result. This option can "
"be used to override `--squash`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:133
msgid "With `--squash`, `--commit` is not allowed, and will fail."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:136
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:170
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:214
msgid "Only useful when merging."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:138
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--verify`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:139
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-verify`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:143
msgid ""
"By default, the pre-merge and commit-msg hooks are run.  When `--no-verify` "
"is given, these are bypassed.  See also linkgit:githooks[5]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:147
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-s <strategy>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:148
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--strategy=<strategy>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:154
msgid ""
"Use the given merge strategy; can be supplied more than once to specify them "
"in the order they should be tried.  If there is no `-s` option, a built-in "
"list of strategies is used instead (`ort` when merging a single head, "
"`octopus` otherwise)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:155
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-X <option>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:156
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--strategy-option=<option>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:159
msgid "Pass merge strategy specific option through to the merge strategy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:160
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--verify-signatures`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:161
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-verify-signatures`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:167
msgid ""
"Verify that the tip commit of the side branch being merged is signed with a "
"valid key, i.e. a key that has a valid uid: in the default trust model, this "
"means the signing key has been signed by a trusted key.  If the tip commit "
"of the side branch is not signed with a valid key, the merge is aborted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--summary`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:173
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-summary`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:176
msgid ""
"Synonyms to `--stat` and `--no-stat`; these are deprecated and will be "
"removed in the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:178
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-q`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:179
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--quiet`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:181
msgid "Operate quietly. Implies `--no-progress`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:182
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-v`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--verbose`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:185
msgid "Be verbose."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:186
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--progress`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-progress`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:192
msgid ""
"Turn progress on/off explicitly. If neither is specified, progress is shown "
"if standard error is connected to a terminal.  Note that not all merge "
"strategies may support progress reporting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:195
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--autostash`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:196
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-autostash`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:203
msgid ""
"Automatically create a temporary stash entry before the operation begins, "
"record it in the ref `MERGE_AUTOSTASH` and apply it after the operation "
"ends.  This means that you can run the operation on a dirty worktree.  "
"However, use with care: the final stash application after a successful merge "
"might result in non-trivial conflicts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:204
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--allow-unrelated-histories`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/merge-options.adoc:211
msgid ""
"By default, `git merge` command refuses to merge histories that do not share "
"a common ancestor.  This option can be used to override this safety when "
"merging histories of two projects that started their lives independently. As "
"that is a very rare occasion, no configuration variable to enable this by "
"default exists or will be added."
msgstr ""
